pst-numeric: arbitrary precision arithmetic, matrices, complex numbers
and numerical methods for PSTricks

Version 1.2, 2026/11/21

pst-numeric is a library of PostScript procedures for PSTricks. Its
decimal numbers (bignums) carry as many significant digits as asked for,
with arithmetic, square roots, exponentials, logarithms, trigonometric
and hyperbolic functions and their inverses, pi, factorials and binomial
coefficients. On top of that it has matrices (determinant, inverse,
linear systems, least squares, symmetric eigenvalues), complex numbers,
roots of functions, integrals and polynomials (values, roots, fitting),
each working on ordinary reals or on bignums. The calculations run in
the PostScript interpreter while the page is drawn, so they can feed
plots directly.

    \usepackage[bignum,calc]{pst-numeric}
    ...
    \psplot{0}{3}{\pstNumeric{[0.5 0 -1] x polyval}}
    \psNumericShow{50 setbnsize pibn}

The package options choose the parts (bignum, trig, matrix, complex,
calc); each part is a separate dvips header. Like every PSTricks package
it needs the latex-dvips route, or xelatex.

Files

  tex/pst-numeric.tex       the package (TeX and LaTeX)
  latex/pst-numeric.sty     LaTeX wrapper
  dvips/pst-numeric*.pro    PostScript headers
  doc/pst-numeric-doc.*     manual (PDF, source and bibliography)
  source/*.ps               the PostScript library the headers are
                            generated from, also usable with Ghostscript
  source/make_headers.py    generates dvips/pst-numeric-*.pro (Python 3)

Install the files of tex/ in tex/generic/pst-numeric/, latex/ in
tex/latex/pst-numeric/ and dvips/ in dvips/pst-numeric/ of a TeX tree.

Repository, tests and bug reports:
  https://github.com/buddyledger/pst-numeric

